---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy — PerkCommons"
  description="What information PerkCommons collects when people submit opportunities or report listings, and how that information is used."
>
  <section class="container py-14">
    <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-brand">Privacy</p>
    <h1 class="mt-2 max-w-3xl text-4xl font-semibold">
      A plain-language privacy notice.
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-5 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-8 text-muted">
      PerkCommons collects limited information needed to operate the public directory,
      display approximate site activity counts, and moderate community submissions and listing reports.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-12 max-w-3xl space-y-10">
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Opportunity submissions</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-muted">
          When you submit an opportunity, PerkCommons collects the information
          entered in the submission form. This may include an optional name or
          email address, details about the opportunity, and notes supplied for
          moderators.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-muted">
          PerkCommons may also collect approximate geolocation, such as a
          country code derived from the request, together with technical
          request information used for moderation and abuse prevention. It
          does not ask for precise device GPS location.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="border-t border-line pt-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Listing reports</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-muted">
          When you report a listing, PerkCommons collects the report reason,
          any details you provide, the affected listing identifier, and an
          optional reporter email address. Similar approximate location and
          anti-abuse information may be processed to protect the reporting
          system from misuse.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="border-t border-line pt-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">How the information is used</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-muted">
          Moderators use submitted information to review opportunities,
          investigate reports, contact a submitter or reporter when necessary,
          correct records, remove records, and protect the service from abuse.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="border-t border-line pt-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">What is public</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-muted">
          Published opportunity records are public. Optional submitter and
          reporter email addresses are not published. Approximate location and
          technical anti-abuse information associated with the person making a
          submission or report are not included in public opportunity records.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="border-t border-line pt-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">First-party public activity counters</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-muted">
          PerkCommons displays the number of unique browsers visiting in the current UTC month,
          browsers active in the previous five minutes, and opportunity pages opened since these
          counters launched. They are approximate browser counts, not unique people or guarantees
          of human engagement. Browsers with tracking protections enabled may not be counted.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-muted">
          Your browser generates a random, first-party ID that is stored locally for the current UTC
          month. Our Cloudflare Worker replaces it with a keyed cryptographic hash before the
          counting database sees it. That database stores neither your raw ID nor your IP address,
          and no third-party analytics scripts are used. We use the IP transiently for rate limits.
          Browser-count records are retained for up to 13 months, activity presence is kept for
          five minutes, and per-listing duplicate prevention lasts 30 minutes. Only totals of
          opportunity opens are kept indefinitely. Do Not Track and Global Privacy Control
          signals disable participation in these counters.
        </p>
        <button type="button" id="site-stats-opt-out" class="mt-4 rounded-md border border-line bg-surface px-4 py-3 font-medium text-ink">Disable anonymous statistics on this browser</button>
        <p id="site-stats-opt-out-status" role="status" class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted"></p>
      </section>

      <section class="border-t border-line pt-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Contact</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-muted">
          Questions or privacy concerns can be sent to
          <a class="font-medium" href="mailto:privacy@perkcommons.com">privacy@perkcommons.com</a>.
          General reports can also be sent to
          <a class="font-medium" href="mailto:hello@perkcommons.com">hello@perkcommons.com</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </section>
  <script>
    const button = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>("#site-stats-opt-out");
    const status = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("#site-stats-opt-out-status");
    button?.addEventListener("click", () => {
      try {
        localStorage.setItem("perkcommons-stats-opt-out", "1");
        for (let i = localStorage.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
          const key = localStorage.key(i);
          if (key?.startsWith("perkcommons-stats-browser-")) localStorage.removeItem(key);
        }
        if (status) status.textContent = "Anonymous activity updates are now disabled on this browser.";
      } catch { if (status) status.textContent = "Your browser blocks local storage; no activity identifier is being stored."; }
    });
  </script>
</BaseLayout>